  "rationale": "The workflow builds a beta on every push to dev with no concurrency control, so repeated pushes can leave redundant in-progress builds running. The P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE pattern (cancel superseded runs) applies: runs share the same workflow and branch, and a newer push supersedes an older in-progress check. Adding a branch-scoped concurrency group with cancel-in-progress cancels only stale dev-branch runs while always letting the latest commit complete fully, preserving build/test coverage and required checks. It adds no secrets, privileges, deployment steps, or new network access. A separate Gradle dependency cache was not added because setup-java cache: 'gradle' already provides an equivalent cache (redundant per the pattern contraindication), and there is no matrix for fail-fast.",
